From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:48:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] the touch census: trap the guest CPU's
 first touch of large IOSurfaces

Off unless REIMS_VGPU_CENSUS is set. Memslots move to a KVM-only view of guest RAM; arms poison
through a user-mode-only userfaultfd; classifies read or write by write-protecting a trapped page
and rerunning its instruction. Observation only: guest pages stay the truth.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
