+/*
+ * LOCAL (Atlas): the touch census. How often does the guest CPU touch large IOSurfaces?
+ *
+ * Observation only: rendering stays in place and the guest's pages stay the truth, so nothing can
+ * go stale. With REIMS_VGPU_CENSUS unset this file makes no mapping, no userfaultfd and no thread.
+ *
+ * Memslots move to a view of guest RAM, the "KVM-only view": a second shared mapping of the same
+ * memfd, which only KVM ever uses. QEMU's devices, NVMe, virtio and every GPU import stay on the
+ * main mapping. No user-mode code here or in QEMU reads through the view: its address lives in
+ * this file and in the memslot, and QEMU's address spaces never see it. So a SIGBUS from a marker
+ * can only come from KVM's fault path inside KVM_RUN, on a vCPU thread. KVM's emulator and other
+ * kernel accesses never raise one: a failed copy becomes KVM_EXIT_MMIO at the RAM's gpa, which
+ * QEMU completes through the main mapping, correctly, or an -EFAULT (below).
+ *
+ * A page's cycle, on userfaultfd opened with UFFD_USER_MODE_ONLY, which vm.unprivileged_userfaultfd
+ * = 0 allows and which needs neither /dev/userfaultfd nor a capability:
+ *
+ *   armed   UFFDIO_POISON. Any guest access: KVM's hwpoison path, SIGBUS with the exact address.
+ *           The vCPU logs the touch, drops the marker and write-protects the page, then runs again.
+ *   held    Write-protected. The same instruction reruns: a read passes, which classifies it. A
+ *           write comes back at once as a bare -EFAULT, no address: the page is this vCPU's
+ *           pending page while RIP has not moved, and it opens.
+ *   open    Nothing on the page.
+ *
+ * A write to a page held since an earlier read gives -EFAULT with nothing to name it, so it
+ * opens every held page and counts one upgrade. Every Nth present the census's thread re-arms
+ * what was touched: WP off, then DONTNEED, then poison. That order matters: MADV_DONTNEED drops a
+ * poison marker but on a file mapping it keeps a uffd-wp one, and POISON refuses a slot that holds
+ * either (EEXIST).
+ *
+ * UFFDIO_POISON and UFFDIO_WRITEPROTECT work on PTEs, so 98k Reims views and the 12 GiB slot add no
+ * VMAs beyond this one mapping: arming splits nothing, and vm.max_map_count sees +1.
+ *
+ * Registering WP makes the view's read faults map read-only (vma_wants_writenotify), so the first
+ * write after a read of each page takes one extra host fault, once per page per mapping.
+ *
+ * Locks: the fault path takes none, and only touches per-page atomics, madvise and uffd ioctls. It
+ * queues no GPU work and calls nothing in Reims. census.lock guards the surfaces, never waits on a
+ * vCPU or the GPU, and is taken only on the rare -EFAULT with no pending page. Each page's word
+ * is the owner's: whoever moves it to ST_WORK alone changes that page's markers.
+ *
+ * A failure must never take the VM with it: an -EFAULT nothing answers disarms the whole census
+ * (census_fuse) before it is allowed to reach QEMU's fatal path.
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+
